\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 Business model\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 Brignole is a small private business. We operate our own websites and advertise only those sites. We do not run an advertising agency. We do not manage Google Ads for other companies, clients, or third parties.\
Websites we own and may advertise with this token (paid Google Ads, billed to Brignole):\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 https://brignole.ch \'97 personal / professional site\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 https://aelle.hiphop \'97 music project and related store\
\ls2\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 https://lunanihongo.com \'97 Japanese language learning site (ready to promote; first paid campaign target)\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 We only advertise websites we own. We do not advertise for anyone else.\
Separately, a nonprofit association (Biography Library) has its own Google Ad Grants account. That Grants account is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  linked to this manager, is 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  billed to Brignole, and will 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  be accessed with this developer token. If API access is needed for Grants, it will be a separate manager account and a separate application.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa287\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 Tool access / use\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 The tool is named 
\f0\b Regia SEO
\f2\b0 . It is a private control panel for one operator (Claudio Brignole).\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls3\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Access: a single shared password and a signed session cookie. There are no public sign-ups, no customer tenants, and no external users.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 No agency, freelancer, or third party can log in. Reports are not sent to an external agency.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The Google Ads part of the panel is 
\f0\b read-only
\f2\b0 . The operator views campaign performance and can prepare a 
\f1\i draft
\f2\i0  of a future campaign (text, keywords, suggested daily budget). Drafts stay inside the panel. The operator then creates or edits the live campaign by hand in the Google Ads web interface.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The tool 
\f0\b does not
\f2\b0  create, pause, enable, or mutate campaigns, ads, budgets, or keywords through the API.\
\ls3\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A nightly scheduled job (once per day) pulls the last days of performance into our own database so the dashboard can load without calling the API on every page view.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 This application is for 
\f0\b Basic Access
\f2\b0  on production accounts owned by Brignole. We do not need Standard Access or Required Minimum Functionality, because the tool is not offered to external advertisers.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa287\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 Tool design\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 High-level flow:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls4\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	1	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 A scheduled job authenticates as a Google Cloud service account that has been invited to the Brignole Google Ads manager / client account.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	2	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The job calls 
\f3\fs25\fsmilli12667 GoogleAdsService.Search
\f2\fs32  (GAQL) against the Brignole client customer ID only.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	3	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Results are stored in our MySQL database (campaign list, daily metrics, keyword-level metrics).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	4	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 The web UI at https://seo.brignole.ch/pubblicita/brignole reads that database and shows a table of campaigns (name, status, clicks, spend, a short written recommendation).\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	5	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Recommendations are computed locally (for example: spend with almost no conversions). They are advice for the operator. They do not write back to Google Ads.\
\ls4\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	6	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 Campaign drafts are stored only in our database. Publishing a live campaign is a manual step in Google Ads, not an API mutate.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 Expected API volume: a few 
\f3\fs25\fsmilli12667 Search
\f2\fs32  requests per night (campaign list, campaign metrics by day, keyword_view by day). Well below Basic Access limits. No user-facing live polling of the API.\
Authentication: service account (Google Cloud) plus this developer token. The token will be sent only from our hosted panel (Hostinger). It will not be embedded in a public website or a mobile app.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa287\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs34\fsmilli17333 \cf2 API services called\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0

\f2\b0\fs32 \cf2 Read-only. We use the Google Ads API REST method:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls5\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 GoogleAdsService.Search
\f2\b0  (
\f3\fs25\fsmilli12667 POST .../customers/\{customer_id\}/googleAds:search
\f2\fs32 )\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 GAQL resources and fields:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 campaign
\f2\b0  \'97 id, name, status; 
\f0\b campaign_budget.amount_micros
\f2\b0 \
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 campaign
\f2\b0  with 
\f0\b segments.date
\f2\b0  and metrics: impressions, clicks, cost_micros, conversions, ctr, average_cpc\
\ls6\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 keyword_view
\f2\b0  \'97 ad_group_criterion.keyword.text, segments.date, impressions, clicks, cost_micros, conversions\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 We do 
\f0\b not
\f2\b0  call mutate methods, including but not limited to:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\ls7\ilvl0\cf2 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 CampaignService / CampaignBudgetService / AdGroupService / AdGroupAdService mutate\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 KeywordPlanIdeaService (not used today)\
\ls7\ilvl0\kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 \outl0\strokewidth0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
\outl0\strokewidth0 \strokec2 any upload, experiment, or conversion-adjust service\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa160\partightenfactor0
\cf2 If we later need write access or Keyword Planner, we will submit an updated use description before changing the tool.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa287\partightenfactor0

